  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `node_content` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Domain]` is on an explicit function with a body. The justification is in fenced citation commentary, as the built-in requires.\n\nThe reason is substantive and matches the source:\n- The test graph implements `outgoing_edges` and `node_path` and scripts only `outgoing_edges` tool calls. It never needs node contents.\n- `Domain` still requires a `node_content` method, so the stub exists only to satisfy the trait.\n- The stub body is `panic!(\"edge inspection must not read node contents\")`. A test that reached it would fail, which is the \"guard\" the commentary describes.\n- The test asserts dependency records (`Dependency::OutgoingEdges`) and the lookup count, so the \"selection dependencies only\" claim holds.\n\nThe function is therefore expected to have zero execution. Reaching it would break the guard, so the exception is justified. The citation is not redundant, and no {impl} or {test} reference appears on the item.",
